    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19e24626_3326623f",
        "filename": "thread/framework/java/android/net/thread/ThreadNetworkController.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-02T10:40:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which errors can happen here? Presumably this can fail if the device is already in ephemeral key mode, or if there is no current thread network, etc. We should specify here which ERROR_xxx codes can happen, and we may need to add new ones. For example, we might have ERROR_EPHEMERAL_KEY_ALREADY_ENABLED/DISABLED, ERROR_EPHEMERAL_KEY_STATE_INVALID, etc.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "b2cbdb1a7bf62c9647c3486288dd5d108febce32",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "38ab39d7_c191d75f",
        "filename": "thread/framework/java/android/net/thread/ThreadNetworkController.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 2024816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-04T07:21:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looked at the implementation again, this only fails when the device is not attached to Thread network. I added to the doc using ERROR_FAILED_PRECONDITION to indicate this.\n\nWhen this is called and there is already an active ephemeral key, we simply generate a new key with the new lifetime and call onResult.",
      "parentUuid": "19e24626_3326623f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "b2cbdb1a7bf62c9647c3486288dd5d108febce32",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dea50a51_60dc3217",
        "filename": "thread/framework/java/android/net/thread/ThreadNetworkController.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-22T09:22:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That doesn\u0027t seem great. If there are two callers that call this at about the same time, one of them might call the method and get the key, then unregister the callback and assume that the key will work. But then right after that the second caller could cause the key to be changed again.\n\nIt seems better to say that if the device is already in ephemeral key mode, then it\u0027s an error to try to activate it again unless it\u0027s deactivated. In that case, even if two callers use the API at the same time, they will both be able to operate, because there will only be one key, and both of them can use it.",
      "parentUuid": "38ab39d7_c191d75f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "b2cbdb1a7bf62c9647c3486288dd5d108febce32",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb7ead44_01e6cde8",
        "filename": "thread/framework/java/android/net/thread/ThreadNetworkController.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 2024816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-02T04:23:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ephemeral key is a temporary single-use code that can be used to establish secure session. It makes sense that only the first call to activate the mode succeeds, and the second call will fail with a `ERROR_BUSY` until the ephemeral key mode is deactivated. Updated the doc and code.",
      "parentUuid": "dea50a51_60dc3217",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "b2cbdb1a7bf62c9647c3486288dd5d108febce32",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a21a5839_36dd14c8",
        "filename": "thread/framework/java/android/net/thread/ThreadNetworkController.java",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-04T09:00:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ERROR_BUSY isn\u0027t the best, because it implies that other operations can\u0027t be used either. But I guess it\u0027s OK if we clearly document it.",
      "parentUuid": "fb7ead44_01e6cde8",
      "range": {
